### 🟡 Important Issues (Should Fix)

#### 4. Hardcoded Passkey Username
**File:** `client/src/components/Wallet/SecuritySettings.tsx` (lines 111 and 157)

`registerPasskey('wallet_user')` uses a hardcoded string instead of the actual `userId` prop. This could cause passkey collisions between users.

**Fix:** Change to `registerPasskey(userId)` in both locations.

#### 5. Unsafe JSON.parse Without Error Handling
**File:** `client/src/lib/securityService.ts` (line 261)

`getSecuritySettings()` directly calls `JSON.parse(stored)` without try/catch. If localStorage is corrupted or contains an older schema, this will throw and crash the wallet UI.

**Fix:** Wrap in try/catch and fall back to defaults:
```typescript
try {
  return JSON.parse(stored);
} catch {
  localStorage.removeItem(SECURITY_SETTINGS_KEY);
  return defaultSettings;
}
```

#### 6. Comment Does Not Match Implementation
**File:** `client/src/lib/securityService.ts` (lines 15-16)

The comment says "SHA-256 hash of PIN" but the actual implementation uses PBKDF2-SHA256 with 100k iterations. Update the comment to reflect the actual (better!) implementation.

